# Mobile First

90%+ of guests open this invitation from mobile messaging apps (WhatsApp, Telegram, Messenger, iMessage). Design for vertical smartphone viewports first — never desktop-first with mobile adaptation.

## Layout & Content

- Storytelling journey optimized for vertical scroll on a phone screen
- Large typography, concise content blocks, clear hierarchy
- Minimize horizontal layouts; avoid desktop-only multi-column patterns
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44px; thumb-driven navigation
- Each section immersive on a single phone screen

## Motion & Performance

- Scroll-triggered reveals and subtle touch feedback replace desktop cursor effects
- Optimize animations for mobile GPUs; prefer `transform` and `opacity`
- When choosing between impressive desktop interaction and better mobile UX, **always prioritize mobile**

## Desktop

Desktop is an enhanced presentation layer built on the mobile experience. Emotional impact, storytelling flow, and core interactions must be fully preserved on mobile without desktop-only effects.
